Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.10,0:00:04.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,“I don't need a stop\Nloss. I just {\c&H1EB0F2&}watch{\c&HFAF7F5&} the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.10,0:00:04.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,chart.”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.80,0:00:07.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,Here's the problem.\NWatching the chart means
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.60,0:00:10.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,you decide to exit while\Nyou're {\c&H1EB0F2&}scared{\c&HFAF7F5&} and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.80,0:00:13.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,losing. That's the worst\Nmoment to decide
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.60,0:00:14.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.30,0:00:17.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,A stop moves that\Ndecision to before the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.50,0:00:19.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,trade, while you're\N{\c&H1EB0F2&}calm.{\c&HFAF7F5&}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.40,0:00:22.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,Without a stop, you\Ncan't know your {\c&H1EB0F2&}risk,{\c&HFAF7F5&}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.60,0:00:24.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,size properly, or\Nmeasure R.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.90,0:00:28.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,If you won't use a hard\Nstop yet, write down
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.90,0:00:31.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,where you're {\c&H1EB0F2&}wrong{\c&HFAF7F5&}\Nbefore you enter. That's
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.70,0:00:32.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,still a plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.20,0:00:35.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,Follow for more beginner\N{\c&H1EB0F2&}mistakes,{\c&HFAF7F5&} explained.
